# To [[serve]]; to [[satisfy]] someone's needs as a [[servant]] would; to [[wait on]].
#: {{syn|en|service#Verb|Thesaurus:serve}}
# To [[diligently]] work on; to pay attention to.
#: {{syn|en|heed|Thesaurus:pay attention}}
#: {{ux|en|You should '''attend to''' your studies if you plan to succeed in the exams.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1947|month=January and February|title=Notes and News: Drivers' Reprisals|journal=Railway Magazine|page=53|text=Some ten years ago, an evening excursion train from the Walsall area to Manchester, when travelling well over the heavily-graded Walsall-Rugeley line, was brought to a stand at a level crossing at Hednesford by the tardiness of a gatekeeper, who was pottering about in his garden instead of '''attending to''' his duties.}}

